We grew up in the slums, surrounded by the tormented souls of both the dead and the living. #speaker: Marcus #portrait:marcus #layout:left #hide:
Our father was never there #speaker: Marcus #portrait:marcus #layout:left
Our mother tried her best, raising a set of twins on her own couldn't have been easy. #speaker: Marcus #portrait:marcus #layout:left
She worked herself to death soon after our 8th birthday #speaker: Marcus #portrait:marcus #layout:left
After that you were my rock, although I was technically older, You raised me. You got us off the streets. Got me this job. #speaker: Marcus #portrait:marcus #layout:left
I owe everything to you. But I dont remember if I had ever said thank you. #speaker: Marcus #portrait:marcus #layout:left
But I guess its too late for that now... #speaker: Marcus #portrait:marcus #layout:left #hide:showPlayer
Emma was a beloved Sister, Fiancé, doctor, and a friend to us all. Good spirits and people alike were drawn to her. #speaker: Nick #portrait:nick #layout:right
Her smile and charm were second to only her determination. #speaker: Nick #portrait:nick #layout:right 
Her determination to, no matter the odds, make a positive impact on those lucky enough to have crossed paths with her. #speaker: Nick #portrait:nick #layout:right
As we know death is not the end for our souls voyage, and as she transcends into her spirited form #speaker: Nick #portrait:nick #layout:right
I know she will continue to make the world itself a better place. #speaker: Nick #portrait:nick #layout:right
